      <eAnnotations source="http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/GenModel">
        <details key="documentation" value="Summary:&#xA;Returns all legal destination moves for the Knight from a given source square, applying&#xA;global rules and Knight-specific movement/blocking rules.&#xA;Algorithm:&#xA;1. Create an empty move list.&#xA;2. For every board square as a candidate destination:&#xA;   - Build a Move(source, destination).&#xA;   - Validate global rules:&#xA;     VacantRule, NilMoveRule, OutOfBoundaryRule, OccupiedRule, FirstNMovesProtectionRule.&#xA;   - If all global rules pass, validate KnightMoveRule.&#xA;   - If KnightMoveRule passes, validate KnightBlockRule.&#xA;   - If all pass, add move to the result list.&#xA;3. Return the collected legal moves.&#xA;Related Features:&#xA;- Piece.player&#xA;- Piece.getLabel()&#xA;- KnightMoveRule.validate()&#xA;- KnightBlockRule.validate()&#xA;- FirstNMovesProtectionRule.validate()&#xA;Related Classes: Game, Move, Place, Rule, KnightMoveRule, KnightBlockRule, FirstNMovesProtectionRule, VacantRule, NilMoveRule, OutOfBoundaryRule, OccupiedRule&#xA;Input:&#xA;- game: current Game instance.&#xA;- source: position of the Knight piece.&#xA;Output:&#xA;- A List&lt;Move> containing all legal Knight moves from source.&#xA;Pre-condition:&#xA;- game is not null.&#xA;- source contains a Knight piece.&#xA;Post-condition:&#xA;- No board state changes.&#xA;- All returned moves satisfy Knight movement and blocking rules."/>
