        <details key="documentation" value="Summary:&#xA;Returns all legal destination moves for the Archer from a given source square.&#xA;Algorithm:&#xA;1. Create an empty move list.&#xA;2. For every board square as a candidate destination:&#xA;   - Build a Move(source, destination).&#xA;   - Validate it against global rules in this order:&#xA;     VacantRule, NilMoveRule, OutOfBoundaryRule, OccupiedRule, FirstNMovesProtectionRule.&#xA;   - If all global rules pass, validate ArcherMoveRule.&#xA;   - If all validations pass, add the move to the result list.&#xA;3. Return the collected legal moves.&#xA;Related Features:&#xA;- Piece.player&#xA;- Piece.getLabel()&#xA;- ArcherMoveRule.validate()&#xA;- FirstNMovesProtectionRule.validate()&#xA;- VacantRule.validate()&#xA;- NilMoveRule.validate()&#xA;- OutOfBoundaryRule.validate()&#xA;- OccupiedRule.validate()&#xA;Related Classes: Game, Move, Place, ArcherMoveRule, FirstNMovesProtectionRule, VacantRule, NilMoveRule, OutOfBoundaryRule, OccupiedRule&#xA;Input:&#xA;- game: current Game instance, used to read board state, configuration, and protection status.&#xA;- source: the board position of the Archer piece.&#xA;Output:&#xA;- A List&lt;Move> containing every legal move available to the Archer from source.&#xA;- The list may be empty if no legal move exists.&#xA;Pre-condition:&#xA;- game is not null.&#xA;- source is not null and is within the board boundary.&#xA;- game.getPiece(source) is an Archer.&#xA;- The board state and configuration are initialized.&#xA;Post-condition:&#xA;- No board state is changed.&#xA;- Returned moves satisfy all global rules and Archer movement rules.&#xA;- Returned moves do not include illegal captures during the protection phase."/>
