  <eClassifiers xsi:type="ecore:EClass" name="KnightBlockRule" eSuperTypes="//Rule">
    <eOperations name="validate">
      <eAnnotations source="http://www.ustb.edu.cn/sei/mde/EnhancedCodeGen">
        <details key="generated" value="true"/>
      </eAnnotations>
      <eAnnotations source="http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/GenModel">
        <details key="documentation" value="Summary:&#xA;Checks whether a Knight’s L-shaped move is blocked by an intervening piece in the Knight’s primary direction.&#xA;Algorithm:&#xA;1. Let source = move.source and destination = move.destination.&#xA;2. Compute dx = |destination.x - source.x| and dy = |destination.y - source.y|.&#xA;3. If the move is not an L-shaped Knight move (dx, dy are not (2,1) or (1,2)), return false.&#xA;4. Determine the blocking square:&#xA;   - If dx = 2 and dy = 1, blocking square = ((source.x + destination.x) / 2, source.y).&#xA;   - If dx = 1 and dy = 2, blocking square = (source.x, (source.y + destination.y) / 2).&#xA;5. Read the piece at the blocking square from the game board.&#xA;6. Return false if the blocking square contains any piece; otherwise return true.&#xA;Related Features:&#xA;- Move.source&#xA;- Move.destination&#xA;- Game.getPiece(Place)&#xA;Related Classes: Game, Move, Place&#xA;Input:&#xA;- game: current game state.&#xA;- move: candidate move to validate.&#xA;Output:&#xA;- true if the Knight’s intermediate blocking square is empty.&#xA;- false if the move is not a valid Knight L-shape or the intermediate blocking square contains any piece.&#xA;Pre-condition:&#xA;- game and move are not null.&#xA;- move.source and move.destination are valid board coordinates.&#xA;Post-condition:&#xA;- No state is changed."/>
        <details key="body" value="// TODO: Please generate a body of this unimplemented method based on the docstring&#xD;&#xA;// TODO: Replace the current body with the generated body &#xD;&#xA;// TODO: Ensure that you mark it @generated NOT after code completion&#xD;&#xA;throw new UnsupportedOperationException();&#xD;&#xA;"/>
      </eAnnotations>
