      <eAnnotations source="http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/GenModel">
        <details key="documentation" value="Summary:&#xA;Determines whether a move violates the early-game protection phase, during which captures are forbidden.&#xA;Algorithm:&#xA;1. Check whether game.numMoves &lt; numProtectedMoves.&#xA;2. If protection is inactive, return true.&#xA;3. If protection is active:&#xA;   - Inspect the destination square.&#xA;   - If destination is occupied, return false.&#xA;   - Otherwise return true.&#xA;Related Features:&#xA;- FirstNMovesProtectionRule.numProtectedMoves&#xA;- Game.numMoves&#xA;- Game.getPiece(Place)&#xA;Related Classes: Game, Move, Place, Rule, Piece&#xA;Input:&#xA;- game: current game state.&#xA;- move: candidate move.&#xA;Output:&#xA;- true if the move is allowed during the current protection status.&#xA;- false if the move attempts a capture during protection.&#xA;Pre-condition:&#xA;- game and move are not null.&#xA;- numProtectedMoves is non-negative.&#xA;Post-condition:&#xA;- No state is changed.&#xA;- The result depends only on the current move count and destination occupancy."/>
        <details key="body" value="// TODO: Please generate a body of this unimplemented method based on the docstring&#xD;&#xA;// TODO: Replace the current body with the generated body &#xD;&#xA;// TODO: Ensure that you mark it @generated NOT after code completion&#xD;&#xA;throw new UnsupportedOperationException();&#xD;&#xA;"/>
