      <eAnnotations source="http://www.eclipse.org/emf/2002/GenModel">
        <details key="documentation" value="Summary:&#xA;Checks whether a move follows Archer movement rules: orthogonal sliding movement, with&#xA;non-capturing moves requiring a clear path and capturing moves requiring exactly one&#xA;intervening piece as the screen.&#xA;Algorithm:&#xA;1. Read source and destination from the move.&#xA;2. Reject if move is not orthogonal:&#xA;   - source.x != destination.x and source.y != destination.y must hold.&#xA;3. Determine whether destination is empty:&#xA;   - If empty, this is a non-capturing move.&#xA;     a. Check every square strictly between source and destination.&#xA;     b. If any square is occupied, return false.&#xA;     c. Otherwise return true.&#xA;   - If occupied, this is a capturing move.&#xA;     a. Check every square strictly between source and destination.&#xA;     b. Count occupied squares.&#xA;     c. Return true only if exactly one intervening piece exists.&#xA;4. Otherwise return false.&#xA;Related Features:&#xA;- Move.source&#xA;- Move.destination&#xA;- Game.getPiece(Place)&#xA;- Game.getPiece(int, int)&#xA;Related Classes: Game, Move, Place, Rule, Piece&#xA;Input:&#xA;- game: current Game instance used to inspect the board.&#xA;- move: candidate move to validate.&#xA;Output:&#xA;- true if the move is a valid Archer move under orthogonal sliding/capture rules.&#xA;- false otherwise.&#xA;Pre-condition:&#xA;- game and move are not null.&#xA;- move.source and move.destination are within or can be tested against the board limits.&#xA;Post-condition:&#xA;- No state is modified.&#xA;- Return value reflects only Archer movement legality."/>
        <details key="body" value="// TODO: Please generate a body of this unimplemented method based on the docstring&#xD;&#xA;// TODO: Replace the current body with the generated body &#xD;&#xA;// TODO: Ensure that you mark it @generated NOT after code completion&#xD;&#xA;throw new UnsupportedOperationException();&#xD;&#xA;"/>
      </eAnnotations>
